# Line endings are part of the contract for the two shell scripts this repository
# ships, so they are pinned rather than left to a checkout's platform defaults.
#
# `rastro-ssh` is run by a POSIX shell on a remote host. Checked out with CRLF it
# fails as `#!/bin/sh^M: no such file or directory`, which names neither the file nor
# the cause. The wrapper already passes `ssh -T` for the same family of reason: CRLF
# translation would corrupt every line of a fingerprint on the way back.
#
# `scripts/*.sh` run inside a Linux container from a bind-mounted checkout, so the
# host's line endings travel into the container unchanged.

* text=auto eol=lf

rastro-ssh text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
